# Source files check out with the line endings this repository stores.
#
# Several tests read a source file and assert on a substring that spans a line, such as
# RaidMarkGestureTests' "gesture = pinchState();\n      cancelPress();". Git's Windows default
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so those assertions failed on the Windows runner and only
# there: one commit was green on `linux` and red on `windows-build` for a reason that had
# nothing to do with the product, which is exactly the kind of noise that gets a Windows gate
# declared unreliable and switched off. Named extensions rather than `*`, so the byte-exact
# golden documents below keep their own rule and nothing under `fixtures/` is implicated.
*.cs text eol=lf
*.axaml text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
docs/THIRD_PARTY_INVENTORY.json text eol=lf
fixtures/licenses/*.json text eol=lf
licenses/*.json text eol=lf
LICENSES/** -text
# Byte-exact golden documents: a checksum covers these bytes, so checkout must never rewrite them.
fixtures/profiles/*.json -text
fixtures/loot-spawns/**/content.json -text
PRODUCT_VERSION text eol=lf
